From 96a8d905be9767552e1b1abe47eaa1c029588e31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Bidlingmaier <bidlingmaier@nvidia.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:07:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] agent: attach exec to the init process cgroup

cgroup v2 rejects processes in inner nodes once controllers are
enabled. systemd and Docker-in-Docker move PID 1 into a child
(init.scope / init), so exec must follow that leaf instead of the
container root.

The previous hardcoded "init/" check only covered DinD. Look up
/proc/<init>/cgroup instead, including the cgroup-namespace view the
agent sees after CLONE_NEWCGROUP. If init has moved outside the
container cgroup, attach to that path.

The rustjail tests cover path classification (nested vs a move out of
the container), /proc cgroup parsing, and live leaf attach when the
cgroup filesystem is writable.

This is a backport to 4.4.0 of the first two commits of the open pull
request kata-containers/kata-containers#13627 (Fixes #10733):

  dc5bda2aae9d agent: attach exec to the init process cgroup
  25d63043a889 agent: add rustjail tests for cgroup v2 nesting

The third commit of the pull request changes only the Kubernetes
integration tests and is not included.

Changes made for the backport:

- Conflicts in cgroups/fs/mod.rs with 4.4.0 and with the previous
  commit are resolved.
- The systemd manager passes the subcgroup to AttachProcessesToUnit
  as an absolute path ("/init.scope"), as the code did before this
  change ("/init/"). systemd refuses a subcgroup path that is not
  absolute, so the relative path of the pull request cannot work.

Signed-off-by: Martin Bidlingmaier <bidlingmaier@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Davanum Srinivas <davanum@gmail.com>
